WEBVTT

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:08.000
The support ship Mihara
is going to look after the Hiei now.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.000
BENTEN                      HAREKAZE

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.220
Thank you.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:15.100
Well, we're going to continue our search
for the missing ships other than the Musashi.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.680
What are you guys going to do?

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.720
What shall we do, Captain?

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.600
The school has instructed us
to search for the Musashi.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.770
If no one objects,
I'd like to continue that search.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.730
Alright. Well said!

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.860
Just don't push yourself too hard.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.200
If you think you're in an impossible situation,
contact us and get out of there.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.490
Strictly speaking, that kind of thing
is our job as the Blue Mermaids.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.250
- Yes, ma'am.
- Captain!

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.500
We're getting information regarding several
sightings of two large unknown ships in the area.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.130
200 nautical miles to the south,
the Admiralty Islands,

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.880
and 300 nautical miles northeast,
towards the Chuuk Islands.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.590
Alright! We'll head for the Chuuk Islands.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.640
Sorry, but would you verify
the nearby Admiralty Islands?

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.180
Understood.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.490
Okay! Let's do this!

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.620
We'll surely get a lot of class credit!

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:22.750
Hey, we might be a little awesome, huh?

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.000
Yeah. The Hiei was a tough ship.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.250
So stopping it makes us awesome, right?

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:29.880
We slew a giant.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.210
Wow!

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.720
<i>- I've got our target.
- Report!</i>

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.970
Its identification band is black and white.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.260
It's a German Deutschland-class
nautical training ship,

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:40.850
<i>the Admiral Spee!</i>

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.500
Now the Spee...

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.330
That was the ship Mina was on, right?

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.670
We had a heck of a time with it, remember?

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.250
That's right!

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.130
What should we do, Captain?

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:39.090
The plan is, um...

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.550
A raid!

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:42.550
Yeah!

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.600
Let's save them!

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:56.690
For my sake...

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.780
HAREKAZE

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.950
What are the specific steps?

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:05.990
Mi, would you explain to everyone what you
told me before, of how to stop the Spee?

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.330
Are you serious about this? Really serious?

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:10.460
Of course!

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:16.460
There's an exposed steam pipe on deck
that's used to heat the fuel buffer tank.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.800
It would be possible for even
the Harekaze to destroy that.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.430
If we break that,
we should be able to stop the ship.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.930
The Spee definitely has less firepower,
armor and speed than the Hiei.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.930
This sounds easy.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:36.060
But it has a small body like a cruiser,
and armor the Harekaze can't pierce.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:41.030
It's equipped with powerful 28 cm cannons
that could sink the Harekaze with a single blow.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:45.120
On top of that, being small
means it has high maneuverability.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.410
It would be very dangerous.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.710
So what shall we do, Captain?

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.540
What do you want to do, Mi?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.340
I...

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:10.640
I want you to help the crew of my ship,
the Admiral Spee, as well as Captain Thea.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:14.940
It would mean exposing everyone
on the Harekaze to danger.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.310
- It'll be okay!
- L-Let's give it a shot!

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.690
- Let's do it!
- Aye!

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:26.200
You underestimate this cruel world once,
you'll regret it for a lifetime.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:31.830
And sometimes, a woman needs guts to put her
life on the line, otherwise she'll lose character.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.210
Alright.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.210
Let's begin the mission!

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.720
Megu, what's the Spee's position?

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:47.470
Ten miles ahead.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.970
Ms. Noma, how do they look?

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.970
Their cannons aren't elevated.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:57.230
It seems like they haven't
detected our presence yet.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.980
Alright. Prepare to attack!

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:14.750
Fourth combat speed!

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.250
Fourth combat speed!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.760
Fool. A little more to the right.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:35.520
So we're in their bridge's blind spot.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.650
Thea, I'm coming now.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.480
Combat. Right torpedo attack,
30 degrees Spee!

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.650
180 degree range, target speed 20 knots,

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:49.450
torpedo speed 52 knots,
oblique angle 0 degrees.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.950
20,000 distance! Long distance torpedo attack!

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:55.870
Four torpedoes, tube one! Give it all you've got!

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.370
You got it!

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:00.750
Ready to fire!

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.500
Commence fire!

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:03.750
Fire!

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.640
The Spee is rotating its main battery!

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.520
Rin, evade! Right full rudder!

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.070
Right full rudder!

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:29.650
When they reduce speed and evade our torpedoes,
we'll target them with our main battery,

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:30.660
so be on the lookout!

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:31.320
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.320
The Spee fired!

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.290
Go back!

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:36.290
Go back!

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.210
Our torpedoes are heading for the Spee!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.960
Now, along with the torpedoes, charge!

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.050
The Spee isn't evading it!

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:47.880
What?!

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:53.180
Main battery!

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:54.300
Aye!

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:07.940
Why aren't they changing course?

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.820
Kayo, get ready for the next one!

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:10.820
Right!

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.370
Damage report!

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:23.750
<i>Number three cannon is seriously damaged!</i>

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.090
<i>Impact on number two cannon! It can still fire!</i>

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.590
Ship is able to put out full power!

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:37.470
They bracketed us!

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.850
Rin! Evade their fire!

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.100
S-Steady as she goes!

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:50.610
All torpedoes passed right under the Spee!

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.360
They didn't evade?

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.950
Then we can't target their weakness!

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:57.120
What should we do?

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.620
Even though the aim was perfect.

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:01.290
The main battery...

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.870
I hate to run away, but...

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:08.630
Then it's impossible to get alongside the ship
and board it. We need to come back.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.010
Mi, don't give up!

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:16.720
But if they hit a small ship like this with
a direct attack, we'll be blown to smithereens.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:19.760
I can't afford to put everyone
in any more danger.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.980
But we made it before, remember?

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.280
Captain, a skipper could probably do it.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:39.830
True, the skipper is small and maneuverable
enough to easily avoid bombardment.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:45.420
But if it gets blown away with
a point-blank shot, the whole mission is over.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:50.800
What shall we do, Captain?

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:55.050
I want to go.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.720
I figured you would say that.

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:00.310
Please go.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:10.440
Roger. For now, Mashiro Munetani,
I hereby give you

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:12.110
command of this ship.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:13.940
Roger!

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.820
Raiding party, get ready!

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.000
First, we draw the Spee's attention to us!

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:33.550
- Yes, ma'am!
- Aye!

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:39.470
30 seconds until we reach the ship.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:40.260
Roger!

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:45.020
20 seconds!

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.640
Sato, when I give the signal, storm the ship!

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:50.480
It's time to show what I got!

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:52.360
Ten seconds!

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.280
Bring the ship 200 meters closer to the Spee!

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.280
Leave it to me!

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.160
Four-three-ready!

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.280
Fire!

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.540
- The captain's there!
- Right on target!

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.920
Now, we just need to distract
the Spee as much as possible!

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:15.420
Deputy-Captain,
secondary battery direct fire course!

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:19.050
Evade it!

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:22.930
Where did we get hit?!

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.140
The radar room, all clear!

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:27.680
No damage to torpedo tube one!

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.810
Torpedo tube two is fine.

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:32.190
Deputy-Captain, it was near
the firing command post!

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:34.610
Firing command post, are you okay?

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:42.870
<i>Ah, I read you.</i>

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:45.240
Ogasawara here. I'm fine.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.700
Takeda here. No problem.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.710
Heki here. I'm all right.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:55.300
I can't put everyone in any more danger.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:11:59.720
Captain. Please handle the Spee.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:04.720
Max speed, the shortest course
out of their range of fire!

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:17.230
How long will it take
to get out of their range of fire?

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:21.280
At max speed, 30 minutes to
get out of range from their main battery,

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:23.280
and 20 minutes from their secondary battery.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:26.410
T-Thirty more minutes?

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:32.000
Operation storehouse four is flooding!

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:45.970
Don't think you can take me down, girls.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:48.350
Macchi is already fighting!

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:49.350
Macchi!

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:05.910
Amazing.

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.910
We were too late.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:11.620
This much water?

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.250
We've got an emergency! Momo!

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:17.880
She's not here! I'm alone!

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:23.260
What should I do? Somebody help me!

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.350
You're from the artillery...

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.560
- We're here...
- ...to help!

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:32.100
We have free time since
the command post blew up.

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:35.100
Everyone, thank you so much!

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:36.980
Let's get this patched up!

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:39.110
Yeah. Tell us what to do.

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:40.860
Okay, over here, please!

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:46.320
Everyone, please hurry
and get out of their range.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.490
There's so many columns of water!

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:52.580
Captain, can't the ship do something,
like a disturbance?

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.750
Shiro and the others are in charge of the ship.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:58.500
We have to be ready for the raiding party
in case something happens to them.

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:02.550
The Harekaze!

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:07.050
Shiro, please protect everyone!

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:10.060
You're not done yet, Captain?

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:22.440
This way!

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:32.870
It's over 90% humidity.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.750
Is the ventilator off?

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:36.040
It's so hot...

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.750
It's over 40 degrees in here.
It's getting dangerous.

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:42.130
We still have to be at max speed?
What's going on outside?

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:44.260
<i>Just a little more. Hang in there!</i>

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:45.630
Ms. Munetani?

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:48.430
<i>I'm in command right now.
And I'm counting on you!</i>

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:50.260
Yes, ma'am. We'll do our best!

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:52.970
- Let's hang tight just a little longer!
- Yeah!

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:55.930
Hey, that's Maron's job!

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:08.780
Marikouji style's naginata technique.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:14.660
If you get hit, it's gonna hurt!

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.130
Whoa, awesome!

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.880
A soldier wins by stumping the enemy.

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:27.760
Huh?

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.140
Isoroku!

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:39.890
We're 11 miles from the Spee, and we're out
of range from their secondary battery!

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:45.900
Not yet? They haven't done it yet?

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:48.530
Ten minutes until we're out of range
from their main battery!

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.280
The bridge is up here!

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:55.830
You're not getting by. I'm protecting Macchi!

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:58.200
So many of you!

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.080
Captain!

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.180
Captain!

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.450
I'm sorry for being late.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.040
Captain, we did it!

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:51.680
Yes!

00:16:55.220 --> 00:17:00.480
Macchi, was I helpful in some way?

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:15.570
That makes ten of them.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:18.490
Well done.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.830
Are you done administering
the antibody, Ms. Minami?

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.340
This is the last one.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.170
Akeno, Mashiro.

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:31.300
Mi!

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.260
"Mi" ?

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.840
I'll introduce you. This is...

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.560
Captain Thea Kreutzer.

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:42.850
She filled me in. You saved all of us
and I'm very grateful.

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.020
I'm Akeno Misaki, captain of the Harekaze.

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:47.400
This is...

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.690
I'm Deputy-Captain Mashiro Munetani.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.780
Is all of your crew safe and sound?

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:55.490
For now. We're going to return
to Seeadler Base and get resupplied.

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:57.490
Then Mi will, too.

00:17:57.990 --> 00:18:00.620
Yes. Naturally, she'll go with us.

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:04.580
For caution, when you return to the base,
I'd like all of you to undergo a full examination.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:05.540
Understood.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.590
Dinner's ready.

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:10.000
It's ready!

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:13.210
Is this lachsfilet?

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:14.760
That's right, Captain.

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:16.680
They call it sushi.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:18.510
We helped, too!

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:24.270
We also made knödel and matjes.

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:27.770
Oh. Sushi, sashimi and karoshi?

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:30.270
I don't think the last one is right.

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:32.530
This is eintopf, right?

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:35.530
That's right, Captain. They call it oden.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:36.860
"Oden" ?

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:41.790
Captain, if you would say a few words.

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:49.290
Through all of our persistent efforts, we have
regained the ship and control of ourselves.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.050
With gratitude towards this auspicious day,

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:55.550
I would like the captain
of the Harekaze to make a toast.

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:57.550
Me?

00:18:58.470 --> 00:18:59.300
Yes.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:05.430
Okay, everyone. Cheers!

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:06.810
Cheers!

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:08.810
Prost!

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:14.980
What should I eat first?

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:26.620
Here, Captain. Aaaah...

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.710
Is that sausage?

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:31.960
It's our ship's special wurst.

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:34.460
I've wanted to eat this for so long!

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.970
It is really good.

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:50.270
Captain. I've been holding on to this for you.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:53.400
Please put it on me.

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:02.740
Ms. Captain...

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:04.910
I'm not crying!

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:10.620
Anyway, your ship is in awful shape.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.080
And whose fault is that?

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:15.630
But it was a nice punch.

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:19.380
Not quite enough to beat us, though.

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:24.140
Why don't you come with us
and get repairs done at Seeadler?

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:28.890
That's okay. We've been told
to rendezvous with the Akashi.

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:32.940
I see. Then this is goodbye.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:33.860
Yes.

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:42.200
I'll return the sake cup, see.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:45.530
From now on, don't think of me
as a member of the Harekaze.

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:50.210
You tellin' me to go home now,
but I can't anymore.

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:01.550
What's wrong?

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:05.550
Coco... I mean, nothing.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:16.440
It was fun!

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.190
For us, too!

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:20.190
Bon voyage!

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:22.610
Gute reise!

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:39.960
I'm goin' on a trip, alright?

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.090
Take care o’ yourself!

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:44.380
Thank you!

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:53.980
You did the kind of work
that doesn't have a payoff.

00:21:58.570 --> 00:22:00.730
And now I'm broke.

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:06.990
Episode 9: Mina in a Pinch!

00:23:39.420 --> 00:23:42.130
Somehow that worked out well, Captain.

00:23:42.590 --> 00:23:47.010
But the Harekaze took so much damage...
